    {
      "id": "zrzguzm",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5.6 Important Forts of Maharashtra"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Maharashtra has over 350 forts, making it the state with the largest number of forts in India. These forts are a testament to the Maratha military genius.",
      "id": "3t3y7ar"
    },
    {
      "id": "lif4w1z",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Fort</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>District</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Importance</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Raigad</p>",
            "<p>Raigad</p>",
            "<p>Capital of Shivaji's kingdom; his coronation (1674) and death (1680) here</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Shivneri</p>",
            "<p>Pune</p>",
            "<p>Birthplace of Shivaji Maharaj (1630)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Sinhagad</p>",
            "<p>Pune</p>",
            "<p>Battle of 1670; Tanaji Malusare died here</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Rajgad</p>",
            "<p>Pune</p>",
            "<p>Shivaji's capital before Raigad for 26 years</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Torna (Prachandagad)</p>",
            "<p>Pune</p>",
            "<p>First fort captured by Shivaji (1645) at age 15</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Purandar</p>",
            "<p>Pune</p>",
            "<p>Treaty of Purandar (1665) signed here with Jai Singh</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Pratapgad</p>",
            "<p>Satara</p>",
            "<p>Battle of Pratapgad (1659); Afzal Khan killed</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Murud-Janjira</p>",
            "<p>Raigad</p>",
            "<p>Unconquered sea fort; controlled by Siddis</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Vijaydurg</p>",
            "<p>Sindhudurg</p>",
            "<p>Shivaji's naval base; 'Gibraltar of the East'</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Sindhudurg</p>",
            "<p>Sindhudurg</p>",
            "<p>Sea fort built by Shivaji; Sindhudurg district named after it</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Daulatabad</p>",
            "<p>Aurangabad</p>",
            "<p>Originally Devagiri; Muhammad bin Tughlaq moved capital here (1327)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Panhala</p>",
            "<p>Kolhapur</p>",
            "<p>Shivaji's escape to Vishalgad (1660); night escape through Pawan Khind</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
